  "body": "### What this PR does / why we need it?\r\n\r\nPacked HCCL layerwise reload can retain owning clones from an earlier chunk and read them on a later slot stream. Slot-local waits do not establish cross-chunk readiness or protect clones while deferred reads are pending.\r\n\r\nKeep Ascend's local packed producer/consumer loops and the engine inheritance already present in main. Record an NPU event after each loader callback and wait for it before the next chunk's unpack/load work. Record owning clones on all supported slot streams and the caller stream before invoking the loader. The tracking helper releases its temporary references before the callback.\r\n\r\nJoin existing caller-stream work onto all slots; retain native HCCL packing/receive boundaries and failure drains. There is no per-chunk post-load host barrier. Callers must join additional-stream work as documented.\r\n\r\nUse main's HCCL-specific metadata cache and session-reset behavior, including its per-model and repeated-update regression tests, for compatibility with both paired main and v0.32.0. IPC behavior is unchanged.\r\n\r\n### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?\r\n\r\nFixes packed HCCL cross-chunk correctness and repeated reloads. No new API or configuration.\r\n\r\n### How was this patch tested?\r\n\r\nAuthor validation on Ascend 910c. Python 3.12.13, torch 2.10.0+cpu, torch_npu 2.10.0.post4; existing native extensions reused. Actual paired main source: `544f182d9f0c9bfe8bd7645525951d5e3692a542`; current release: v0.32.0.\r\n\r\n- After merging main `91db901e4`, weight-transfer UT: **167 passed** for each of paired main and v0.32.0. Coverage includes scalar/empty/mixed-dtype payloads, ordering, lifetime tracking, per-model metadata reuse/session reset, failure cleanup, and immediate clone release by the loader. Release validation uses tag `5df63a7203` with generated package version metadata set to 0.32.0; native binaries are reused.\r\n- Real two-process HCCL: **6/6 updates correct for each of paired main and v0.32.0**, 2/3 buffers, 16 chunks per update.\r\n- Native delayed-clone stress: **10/10 correct**; allocator-pressure stress: **10/10 correct**, zero unsafe reuse. These use real NPU operations with a simulated collective through the worker path.\r\n- Local packed model/graph regression: **2 passed in 524.55s**, four-layer Qwen3.5-35B-A3B MoE, FULL_DECODE_ONLY, 2/3 buffers, four updates each; generation text and token logprobs exactly match an independent startup reference. This is selected-layout validation, not full-depth or long-duration serving acceptance.\r\n- Ruff/format, spelling, applicable Linux source checks, and mypy Python 3.10/3.11/3.12 passed. Full `bash format.sh ci` was attempted on Windows; some shell/tool-dependent hooks could not complete. Hardware CI remains required.\r\n\r\nThe final self-review changes add type annotations, active-stream assertions, a clone-release regression, and clarify comments; no packed data-plane behavior changed after the native/model run. The migrated commit preserves the verified source tree; the final follow-up only updates this PR number in test comments/skip text.\r\n\r\nServing throughput, long-run performance and release-pairing model E2E remain unvalidated. No performance improvement claim.\r\n\r\n```bash\r\npython -m pytest -q tests/ut/distributed/weight_transfer\r\nVLLM_RL_TEST_DEVICE_INDEX=10 python -m pytest -vv -s --tb=short \\\r\n  tests/e2e/pull_request/two_card/rlhf/state_transitions/test_hccl_weight_transfer.py \\\r\n  -k packed_cross_chunk\r\n```\r\n\r\n\nLatest main refresh: `8fecfe122`. Resolve the two metadata-related conflicts using main's implementation/tests, remove the duplicate branch cache, and retain the local packed event fix. Ruff/format, spelling/workflow lint, applicable Linux source checks and mypy 3.10/3.11/3.12 pass. Main and v0.32.0 UT each pass (167 tests). Native/model tests were rerun on this exact head after the merge (see the 2026-10-28 validation below).\n\n### 2026-10-28 validation after main refresh\n\nRe-ran author hardware validation at Ascend `8fecfe122bb589e4903e588a72cdcb10ac1047f4`. Verified latest main still pins vLLM `544f182d9f0c9bfe8bd7645525951d5e3692a542`; created fresh isolated source worktrees and regenerated vLLM version metadata with setuptools_scm: `0.32.1rc1.dev350+g544f182d9`. Imported source paths, Git revisions, tracked cleanliness and changed-file SHA256 were checked. Existing native binaries were reused; original installed sources were preserved.\n\n- Main and v0.32.0 UT: **167 passed each**.\n- Real two-process HCCL: **6/6 correct per pairing**, 2/3 buffers, 16 chunks/update.\n- Real NPU delayed-clone and allocator-pressure controls: **10/10 correct each**, zero unsafe reuse. Callback-derived-state control: **10/10 correct**.\n- Independent negative controls: removing only the event wait, removing only clone tracking, or recording completion before the callback each produces **0/10 correct** in its corresponding stress case. The mechanism tests use a simulated collective with real NPU work through the worker path.\n- Paired-main model/graph E2E: **2 passed in 524.55s**, all eight reload signatures match the independent startup reference exactly. Test processes exited and source worktrees remain clean.\n\nRelease-pairing model E2E, full-depth/long-duration serving and serving-performance validation remain pending; this run does not claim performance improvement.\n\n- vLLM main: https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/544f182d9f0c9bfe8bd7645525951d5e3692a542\n",
